# T-1845 — accidentally-tracked bloat from T-1834 incident investigation.
# *.db are runtime sqlite indexes (fw-vec-index.db = 78MB).
#
# The `/os` and `/sys` entries that used to sit here are DELIBERATELY GONE (T-2990).
# They ignored two ImageMagick PostScript files (36MB + 14MB) written into the repo
# root, on a recorded guess — "some convert/magick call writes a bare extensionless
# output name" — that turned out to be wrong, and with the note "root-cause task
# pending". No such task was ever filed, so the guess stood for three months while
# the ignore rule removed the one signal that would have prompted anyone to check.
#
# Two more instances followed (`yaml,sys` 6.8MB on 2026-08-08, `yaml` on 2026-08-12).
# They were NOT covered by these rules, showed up in `git status` as `??` for days,
# and still nobody looked — but the first two were invisible even to that.
#
# The real cause was the framework's own P-011 gate: it runs each LINE of
# `## Verification` as a separate shell command, so a `python3 -c "` block written
# across several lines has its PYTHON BODY eval'd as bash, where `import yaml,sys`
# reaches ImageMagick's screenshot tool and writes to the repo root. See T-2990's
# RCA. Prevention is a preflight in lib/verification-port.sh; detection is a
# `fw doctor` rail. Neither needs an ignore rule, and an ignore rule here would
# blind the git-status surface again — which is why these two are not coming back.
.context/working/*.db
.context/working/*.db-shm
.context/working/*.db-wal
.context/working/*.db-journal
.context/working/*.db.manifest.json
.context/working/*.db.reindex.lock
.context/working/*.db.reindex.resume
# T-3058: the reindex SCRATCH copy and its journal. `.reindex.resume` above was
# already here, and `web/embeddings.py:1092` moves the scratch into that exact
# path — the two are the same file at different moments of one run, and only one
# of them was ignored. The scratch is not a leak: a bootstrap resumes across
# hourly cron firings for 29-58h (OBS-258), so it sits in .context/working/ for
# days, at index size (1.7GB here), inside the directory every handover commits
# from. Staged once by `git add -A .context`, refused by the T-1845 large-file
# guard. Kept narrow — `.db.reindex.*` would work but the T-2990 note above is
# about ignore rules that blind git-status, so these name only what they cover.
.context/working/*.db.reindex.*.tmp
.context/working/*.db.reindex.*.tmp-journal
.context/working/.agent-dispatch-counter

# Child-2 write-out staging proposals (T-2539) — generated, not tasks; regenerable via `fw bpmn compile --write`
.context/bpmn-staged/

# T-2734: generated at test time by tests/unit/test_bvp_cli_*.py (tmp.write_text)
tests/unit/_bvp_cli_imported*.py

# T-3038 (OBS-291): per-worker session-scoped focus files. Ephemeral worker
# state — the shared .context/working/focus.yaml stays tracked, these do not.
.context/working/focus.*.yaml
